{"base_manifest_sha256":"531f85386978d805de3756d2d1c70d748a4cd392c0caad3c4173e8a9d9c6fa06","language_manifest_sha256":"08a8a13a55bf96b1d2a3ddc32d5d1c945c1a9a57dea8e17a194a83ea58a1cb14","review":{"author":"Codex","basis":"User-approved scalar function/if-expression model from pinned wiki artifacts; incomplete older sources are explicitly reconstructed.","date":"2026-10-21","decisions":["Enable global arrow definitions, scalar inferred/typed parameters, positional/named required arguments, multiline last-expression returns and value-if in every v1-v6 profile.","Global captures refer to bindings visible at definition; reading them requires initialization before the call. Caller locals are not captured. Globals and parameters cannot be reassigned by a function; locals may be shadowed and reassigned.","Forward calls are allowed in an acyclic static graph. Recursion, nested definitions, overloads, parameter defaults, tuple returns, methods and first-class functions are outside this release.","Each written call chain gets independently specialized bindings, parameters, var and stateful builtin call sites. History follows the already pinned bar-aligned model, including holes and final variable values.","Argument expressions execute once in source order before parameter initialization. Function result qualifier conservatively includes all arguments and body dependencies.","Value-if executes only one branch, checks both, promotes int/float returns, and synthesizes numeric na, legacy bool na or v6 false when else is absent. String-valued if requires else.","Unused definitions receive structural/name/write/cycle checks; type specialization is performed at each reached-in-source call, including calls in statically unchosen branches. Limits bound compile expansion and IR admission."],"external_pine_execution":false,"test_refs":["tests/test_functions.py","conformance/functions/cases.json"]},"schema_version":"openpine.function-spec.1","series_manifest_sha256":"98be9070ef98dff218547